KIMEI Global

Mobile React Native Developer (Middle) 

About the job
KIMEI Global is on a mission to become a leading software outsourcing service provider in the region, serving clients in Japan, Hong Kong, Taiwan, APAC, and North America. We place humans at the core of our development, fostering a culture of mutual respect and support. Our core services include offshore development, software maintenance, E-commerce, and the Salesforce ecosystem.



Our core services offering includes:

Offshore development
Software maintenance & support
E-commerce development
Salesforce ecosystem
Employee Supply


Job Description

Produce fully functional mobile applications by writing clean, modularized, and reusable React Native code.
AI-Enhanced Development: Leverage AI coding assistants (e.g., GitHub Copilot, Cursor) to accelerate development cycles, refactor code, and ensure high-quality output.
Collaborate with designers, product managers, and backend engineers to transform product visions into reality.
Troubleshoot, debug, and optimize application performance for a seamless user experience across iOS and Android.
Research and suggest new mobile products, applications, and protocols to stay ahead of technology trends.
Design and improve interfaces to enhance user experience.
Ensure both new and legacy applications meet strict quality standards.


Requirements

Education: Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science or an equivalent field.
English: Fluent
Experience: At least 2+ years of experience in mobile application development with a strong focus on React Native.
AI Proficiency: 

Strong interest or proven experience in using AI tools (LLMs, AI-driven debugging) to improve coding efficiency and problem-solving.
Technical Skills: 

Understanding of React Native libraries (Redux, MobX, etc.).
Expertise in handling platform-specific code for iOS and Android.
Experience with POS machines and payment device integration.
Strong experience in integrating WebRTC, VoIP, and Socket.io for real-time communication features.
Proficiency in handling real-time activities and in-app notifications.
Testing & CI/CD: Experience with unit testing frameworks (e.g., Jest), mobile testing tools (e.g., Detox), and CI/CD pipelines.
Soft Skills: Excellent analytical skills, a proactive problem-solving attitude, and the ability to perform well in a team environment.
Portfolio: A demonstrable portfolio of released applications on the App Store or Google Play.


